 'trapped-cash':[['Why can a group surplus hide a local shortage?','Resources may be in another entity or currency and unavailable before the obligation falls due.'],['What can block a transfer?','Legal restrictions, regulation, tax, collateral location, operational limits or cut-off times.'],['Does more cash at entity B always solve entity A’s problem?','Only the transferable amount available before the deadline helps A.'],['What should a group liquidity report show?','Locations of resources and obligations, transfer limits, currencies and stress assumptions.']],
 stress:[['Why combine rather than isolate shocks?','Deposit outflows, refinancing failure and margin calls can occur at the same time.'],['What makes a management action credible?','Available capacity, unique resources, named owners, tested execution and settlement before the need.'],['Why could sale proceeds be overstated?','Market discounts, sale limits, encumbrance or delayed settlement may reduce usable cash.'],['Does positive aggregate headroom end the analysis?','No. Check the path through time, currencies, entities, operational constraints and capital effects.']],
 'reverse-stress':[['How is reverse stress different from a normal scenario?','It starts with a failure threshold and finds the events required to reach it.'],['Is the calculated threshold a probability?','No. Plausibility and likelihood require additional evidence.'],['What does a negative break-even withdrawal share mean?','Other calls already exceed resources before deposit withdrawals begin.'],['What should follow the calculation?','Assess plausible pathways to the threshold and credible actions that move it further away.']],
